.TH SDL_HINT_BMP_SAVE_LEGACY_FORMAT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_BMP_SAVE_LEGACY_FORMAT \- Prevent SDL from using version 4 of the bitmap header when saving BMPs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_BMP_SAVE_LEGACY_FORMAT \(dqSDL_BMP_SAVE_LEGACY_FORMAT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The bitmap header version 4 is required for proper alpha channel support and SDL will use it when required\[char46] Should this not be desired, this hint can force the use of the 40 byte header version which is supported everywhere\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Surfaces with a colorkey or an alpha channel are saved to a 32-bit BMP file with an alpha mask\[char46] SDL will use the bitmap header version 4 and set the alpha mask accordingly\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Surfaces with a colorkey or an alpha channel are saved to a 32-bit BMP file without an alpha mask\[char46] The alpha channel data will be in the file, but applications are going to ignore it\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

